CloudBurrow patch 2 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the bug: #1124).

The bug: a REPEATED field a streamed row (tabledata.insertAll) left out was
stored NULL, so `tags IS NULL` read true, ARRAY_LENGTH(tags) NULL and
ARRAY_TO_STRING(tags, ',') NULL; a REPEATED field given as null was refused
("invalid value type <nil> for ARRAY column"), at the top level and inside a
RECORD. In BigQuery a stored array is never NULL: "each array is written as
an empty array" when written to a table (array type,
https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/data-types#array_type).
The patch writes an empty array for a REPEATED column a row leaves out in
Repository.AddTableData, which every write of rows goes through (insertAll,
the Storage Write API, loads, a query's destination table), and for a
REPEATED field given as null, or left out of a RECORD, in
types.normalizeData. server/repeated_empty_test.go (insertAll and a JSON
load) and types/repeated_empty_test.go fail without the patch and pass with
it.

